{
 "schema": "fd-ct-5b-periods/1",
 "labels": {
  "what": "5B, descriptive: the per-period (e) data unfolds of 1A-1F, 1G/1L/1M and 1N-1P on the 16 cells, each over its own MC truth (the double ratio), against each other (not against ALL, whose committed integrals would make a ratio absolute), with a noise reference of 10 bootstrap replicas per period (refit per replica; (e)'s seed term is zero by construction, S1-DIRECTOR-RULINGS.md section 2); chi2 values are distances in the reported matrix's metric beside their noise expectation, not tests",
  "cpl": "C_PL,5D by 2D's DESIGN section 2 on the 16 cells, relative to each cell: built from the observed offsets, so it contains them by construction and cannot fail; three periods, about 1.83 effective dof; printed beside the reported matrix, not in it (LIMITATION-PLAN-ADDENDUM-20261028.md section 5.4)",
  "vs_5a": "5B's period offsets g_X against 5A's projection of the 2D offsets (fd_ct_period.json, variant central): the difference is where 5A's assumption (the offset does not depend on E_avail, q3 or W inside a 2D bin) and 5D's own unfold disagree; 5A's g carries 2D's noise, which has no reference here",
  "contrast": "the p_parallel contrast across 4.5 GeV/c, the only p_parallel boundary of the 16 cells; it is not 2D's step near 8 GeV/c, which lies inside the cells' [4.5, 60) range, so a 2D-like step is diluted in it",
  "no_threshold": "no consistency threshold is declared; whether the periods agree is read by the director and Joseph from the chi2 beside its noise draws",
  "not_citable_for": [
   "the cause of a period difference, or which period is right",
   "a validated size: a block built from the observed differences contains them by construction",
   "a covariance component or a change to the reported matrix or to kappa",
   "a coverage or calibration statement"
  ]
 },
